v 0.11
- Added `aperi-session`, a session helper to be run by a systemd user unit
  (`aperi-session.service`). It replaces `aperi_fm1` and
  provides both the org.freedesktop.FileManager1 ShowItems service and the
  removal of wine file associations as soon as they are created. Either
  feature can be disabled with `--no-fm1` / `--no-wipewine`. It can also run without
  systemd (e.g. `exec aperi-session --exit-with-session` in sway config): only
  one instance per user runs, and `--exit-with-session` makes it exit together
  with the Wayland compositor
- `meson install` now installs the `aperi-session` systemd user unit, the
  desktop entry, documentation and examples
- The global configuration directory follows the configured sysconfdir
- Tests can be run with `meson test`
- Added a PKGBUILD for Arch Linux
- Added `aperi-setup`, to configure a user account to use aperi and aperi-session
- Rewritten the `aperi(1)` man page and added `app-chooser(1)`, `aperi-session(1)`
  and `aperi-setup(1)`; all are installed by meson

v 0.10.1
- Fixed a bug when multiple %f were present in a single argument
- Minor fixes

v 0.10.0
- Added support for specific URIs like https://youtu.be/
- Added `aperi_fm1` program to handle org.freedesktop.FileManager1 ShowItems requests
- `app-chooser`: added support for URI arguments

v 0.9.0
- Added support for /etc/aperi global config directory
- Fixed a couple of memory leaks

v 0.8.0
- Removed deprecated `*` rule

v 0.7.2

- Add a missing check when handling URI rules

v 0.7.1

- Fixed bug where not URI rules could be applied to URI arguments

v 0.7

- Honor XDG_CONFIG_HOME variable, if present, to find the config directory
- Deprecated '*' rule, replaced by '/*' rule
- Added support for placeholders in launcher rules
- Added support for quoting via `"` in configuration file, to enable the use
of `,` and `=` in rules patterns and of spaces in command arguments

v 0.6

- Added output of the version number to the usage string

v 0.5

- Implemented percent decoding of file:// uris

v 0.4

- Added support for multipart extensions, like .tar.gz
- Fix: prevent rules from matching shorter extensions (abcd= matched .abc)
- Fixed aperi.desktop file to handle uris
- Improvements in README.md

v 0.3

- Removed `gtk4-open` helper and substituted with `app-chooser`
- Changed configuration path from .config/aperi.cfg to .config/aperi/config
